{"availability":"available","full":"firecrawl/pdf-inspector","name":"pdf-inspector","description":"Fast Rust library for PDF inspection, classification, and text extraction. Intelligently detects scanned vs text-based PDFs to enable smart routing decisions.","category":"Productivity","language":"Rust","stars":19466,"forks":1317,"created":"2026-02-06T19:44:47Z","updated":"2026-09-30T23:28:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://firecrawl.github.io/pdf-inspector/","topics":["markdown","nodejs","ocr-routing","pdf","pdf-classification","pdf-extraction","pdf-parser","python","rust","text-extraction"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","stars":19466,"forks":1317}],"technologies":["Node.js","Python","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fast Rust library for PDF classification and text extraction. By default it detects whether a PDF is text-based or scanned, extracts text with position awareness, and converts to clean Markdown without OCR. Native Rust and CLI consumers can opt into selective OCR. Includes bindings for Python, Node.js, and browser WebAssembly.","Built by Firecrawl to handle text-based PDFs locally in under 200ms, skipping expensive OCR services for the 54% of PDFs that don't need them.","pdf-inspector was built for pipelines that process PDFs at scale. Instead of sending every PDF through OCR:"],"features":["Smart classification — Detect TextBased, Scanned, ImageBased, or Mixed PDFs in 10-50ms by sampling content streams. Returns a confidence score (0.0-1.0) and per-page OCR routing.","Text extraction — Position-aware extraction with font info, X/Y coordinates, and automatic multi-column reading order. Rotated runs (margin stamps, chart axis titles) keep a true axis-aligned box and report their…","Markdown conversion — Headings (H1-H4 via font size ratios), bullet/numbered/letter lists, code blocks (monospace font detection), tables (rectangle-based and heuristic), bold/italic formatting, URL linking, and page…","Table detection — Dual-mode: rectangle-based detection from PDF drawing ops, plus heuristic detection from text alignment. Handles financial tables, footnotes, and continuation tables across pages.","CID font support — ToUnicode CMap decoding for Type0/Identity-H fonts, UTF-16BE, UTF-8, and Latin-1 encodings."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/pdf-inspector/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"412d70d7ee16302a4452eff75f7a985296f271cecf82a5c2a6f6ebbea3134c5d","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Fast Rust library for PDF classification and text extraction. By default it detects whether a PDF is text-based or scanned, extracts text with position awareness, and converts to clean Markdown without OCR. Native Rust and CLI consumers can opt into selective OCR. Includes bindings for Python, Node.js, and browser WebAssembly.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/pdf-inspector/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"pdf-inspector was built for pipelines that process PDFs at scale. Instead of sending every PDF through OCR:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/pdf-inspector/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"412d70d7ee16302a4452eff75f7a985296f271cecf82a5c2a6f6ebbea3134c5d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/pdf-inspector/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-30T23:28:35Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/pdf-inspector/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:06:50.166Z","hash":"412d70d7ee16302a4452eff75f7a985296f271cecf82a5c2a6f6ebbea3134c5d","originalBytes":13799,